2026-09-20: next-read spill selection, not a coalescing-policy change.

EvoMIR section 7 already requires the furthest NEXT use. The previous scan
compared final interval endpoints. The 27-register MIR RED expected victim
1 but selected 0, with no Rust compilation error. A second test ensures a
victim cannot lend a register reserved for a later fixed operand. Both pass;
the MIR library has 7 passing tests. The selected floating, inline-assembly,
allocation-verifier and linear-scan integration suites have 34 passing tests.
Lowest-free assignment, call/clobber exclusions and no-coalescing remain.
